<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10121"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 6:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found this info on the Rader family. <BR> <BR>  <BR>Father- William E. Rader &#40;deceased, 1996&#41; <BR>Mother- Dorothea M. Rader <BR>Brothers- Paul &#40;1947&#41;, Bill Rader &#40;1949&#41;, Jeff &#40;1955&#41;, <BR> <BR>Obituary &#40;Wichita Eagle on Dec. 29, 1996&#41; <BR>William E. &#34;Bill&#34; Rader,74, retired KG&amp;E Ripley Generating Station plant operator; died Friday, Dec. 27, 1996. Survivors: wife, Dorothea: sons, Dennis, Jeff, both of Wichita, Paul of Falun, Bill of Climax; brothers, Ted of Wichita, Don of Grove, OK, Wallace of Mitchell, IN; eight grandchildren. <BR> <BR>1948-1963 William E. Rader, held various positions for KG&amp;E Fireman, lineman, etc. <BR>1960 Dorothea M. Rader, bookeeper, Leekers IGA <BR>  <BR>   <BR>This means that the brothers in 1974 would bee: <BR> <BR>Paul:27 years <BR>Bill &#40;william&#41;: 25 <BR>Jeff &#40;jerrery&#41; : 19 <BR> <BR>SO it is possible that some of thise brothers were the &#34;dude´s&#34; BTK wrote about in his letter. <BR>Did BTK want to save his brothers? <BR>OR did his brothers want to, or was threthened to, save Dennis? <BR> <BR>I am grasping at straws, I know, but I cantlet it go for som reason... <BR> <BR>Any thoughts?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
